{"cuisine/hakka-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/hakka-cuisine","n":"Hakka cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in China","intro":[["Hakka cuisine is the cooking style of the Hakka people. It is found primarily in the Chinese provinces of Guangdong, Fujian, and Jiangxi, as well as parts of Taiwan and within countries with significant overseas Hakka communities.  There are many restaurants in mainland China, Taiwan, Hong Kong, Indonesia, Malaysia, Singapore, and Thailand, as well as in the United States and Canada, that serve Hakka food. Hakka cuisine was listed in 2014 on the first Hong Kong Inventory of Intangible Cultural Heritage."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"hakka-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hakka_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"The Hakka Cookbook (blog)","ref":"site/thehakkacookbook-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thehakkacookbook.com","note":"Linda Lau Anusasananan's companion blog with Hakka recipes and news.","url":"https://thehakkacookbook.com/tag/hakka-recipes/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"The Hakka Cookbook: Chinese Soul Food from around the World","ref":"cookbook/the-hakka-cookbook-chinese-soul-food-from-around-the-world","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Linda Lau Anusasananan, 2012","note":"University of California Press book on Hakka cooking in China and the diaspora, by a former Sunset food editor.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/9780520273283","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Dishes","count":1,"links":[["Yueguangbing","dish/yueguangbing"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/97/Suan_Pan_Zi.jpg/500px-Suan_Pan_Zi.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"jiathwee","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/lice